From f3b26bee4e5c0c88b218d0e6153df88881e2e708 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:10:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(4leaf): chessmen face their walking direction;
 original attack frame; no borrowed faces

Direction and action (genesis-chessman-actors.js, game.js)
- Every reviewed 37-frame OBS member shares one layout in the extracted
  indices: 0-2 rear three-quarter, 3-7 rear body with alternating legs,
  10 rear weapon raise, 18 front three-quarter strike/cast, 25-30 front
  body with alternating legs. Checked on six members side by side, then
  per member at 2x.
- drawGame() now records the screen direction of each DMP step. Moving up
  the board plays the rear walk 3..7 (35 members); moving down keeps the
  front cycle. Before, every chessman walked backwards with its face to the
  camera, and unreviewed ones spun through 0..7 in both directions.
- attack plays front -> 18 -> 18 -> front for 39 members (was 3).
- 22 more members get the reviewed front idle/walk (frames 25/30), total 42.
- Excluded: 0042 (4-7 not extracted), 0058 (3-7 are sword poses),
  0069/0079 (rear unclear), 0084/0085 (non-humanoid), 0045 (front is 18).
- Evidence level INFERRED (visual review). The original action table and
  frames 8,9,11-17,19-24,31-36 are still not extracted.

Portraits (game.js imageFor)
- Removed the invented (sourceId%59)+1 formula. On main it put 35 CardData
  faces on 78 different cards. Removed the two entries giving one face to
  two characters. Unsourced cards show the original IMG.pak card back.

Tests: new actor-direction-attack-score.cjs and card-portrait-integrity.cjs
check rendered frames/sources; five tests that pinned the old behaviour now
cover unreviewed members (0067/0068/0074/0087) and accept the card back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
